Object.assign(E.preview,{"fc-20261120-01": "Athletic return to San Mames with three wins, a draw and one defeat in their last five competitive matches. Victories over Getafe and Real Sociedad give the hosts grounds for confidence, while their 16 points put them seventh. Espanyol are 13th on 12 points and have won only one of five, although beating Villarreal and then holding Deportivo without conceding suggests defensive improvement. Athletic should therefore avoid forcing the game and exposing space behind their attacks. Their stronger recent winning record and home advantage nevertheless make Athletic Club my selection.", "fc-20261120-02": "Bayern welcome Vincent Kompany back to the touchline while seeking to strengthen their lead. They have 21 points from nine unbeaten league games and four wins plus a draw in their last five competitive outings. Cologne are 15th on nine points and winless in four league matches, leaving them vulnerable to sustained pressure at the Allianz Arena. Manuel Neuer, Serge Gnabry and Alphonso Davies are among Bayern's absentees, but the hosts have scored 20 goals in four home league games. Jamal Musiala's possible return is encouraging. Bayern's pressing, attacking depth and home dominance make Bayern Munich my selection.", "fc-20261120-03": "This meeting of the bottom two gives Troyes an important home opportunity. They are 17th with eight points after ten matches and remain short of goals, but clean sheets against Toulouse and Le Mans show that defensive organisation can bring results. Le Havre are last on two points, have no league win and have lost all five of their latest competitive matches. Heavy concessions against Marseille and PSG underline the visitors' difficulties. Troyes should build pressure patiently rather than overcommit. Neither side inspires complete confidence, but home advantage and the stronger league record make Troyes my selection.", "fc-20261120-04": "Only three points separate sixth-placed Bielefeld, on 17, from fourth-placed Magdeburg, on 20. The hosts have beaten Braunschweig and Holstein Kiel in successive league games and return home with confidence. Magdeburg's convincing win over St Pauli confirms their attacking danger, but their recent results also include a heavy cup defeat at Bayern. Bielefeld should resist turning this into an uncontrolled exchange and instead protect midfield space. Their consecutive league wins and home advantage make Arminia Bielefeld my selection.", "fc-20261120-05": "Darmstadt need to restore both their scoring threat and defensive stability. They are 17th on nine points and have recently lost to Nuremberg and heavily to Karlsruhe. Heidenheim are seventh on 16 points, although three draws and two defeats in five mean their higher position should not be mistaken for strong form. Scoring twice against Hannover in their latest draw offers encouragement, particularly against an unsettled home defence. This looks close rather than straightforward, but Heidenheim's stronger season record and opportunity to exploit Darmstadt's weaknesses make Heidenheim my selection.", "fc-20261120-06": "Molde's high-scoring matches reveal defensive problems as well as attacking strength. Their latest draw with Sandefjord involved five goals conceded, a vulnerability second-placed Bodo/Glimt can target. Molde have 44 points in fifth, compared with the visitors' 62. Bodo/Glimt have won their last two league matches against Viking and Tromso and also kept Lille scoreless in Europe. Both attacks can open the game up, but the visitors' stronger season-long record and ability to exploit space make Bodo/Glimt my selection.", "fc-20261120-07": "AGF's clean-sheet win over Horsens provides a useful foundation. Eighth on 15 points, the hosts have two wins, two draws and a defeat in five competitive matches, including a goalless European draw with Braga. Lyngby are tenth on 11 points and have lost three of five, most recently failing to score against Silkeborg. Their win over Randers and scoring threat against Nordsjaelland mean AGF must still protect against counters. Better recent defensive control and home advantage make AGF my selection.", "fc-20261120-08": "Cercle Brugge have regained confidence through successive wins over Antwerp and La Louviere, the latter with a clean sheet. Three earlier defeats show that the recovery still needs consolidation. Westerlo's last two games brought heavy concessions against Anderlecht and Charleroi, making defensive repair urgent. Their earlier wins confirm attacking potential, so Cercle should avoid an unnecessarily open match. With improving defensive confidence and home advantage, Cercle Brugge are my selection.", "fc-20261120-09": "Verona's unbeaten five-match run is built on defensive stability. They beat Juve Stabia and Carrarese without conceding before drawing scoreless with Mantova, giving them three consecutive clean sheets. Fifth place on 16 points looks much higher than Cesena's 12th, but only one point separates them. Cesena have recently beaten Empoli and Catanzaro and deserve respect. Verona's ability to protect their goal can nevertheless allow a small number of chances to decide the match. Home advantage and defensive consistency make Hellas Verona my selection.", "fc-20261120-10": "Andorra's home advantage is offset by poor league results. They are 21st on 11 points and have recently lost to Girona, Burgos and Almeria while also conceding twice in a draw with Tenerife. Leganes are 16th on 15 points and remain inconsistent, but have won their last cup match and then beaten Burgos in the league. Their earlier heavy concessions against Valladolid and Albacete prevent a confident defensive assessment. Both sides have weaknesses, yet the visitors' return to winning form makes Leganes my selection.", "fc-20261120-11": "Annecy's stronger league position needs to be weighed against two consecutive heavy league defeats to Montpellier and Boulogne. They are ninth on 16 points, while their cup advancement came on penalties after a drawn match rather than a clear playing-time victory. Clermont are 15th on 11 points and have drawn frequently, but their latest league win over Rodez came with a clean sheet and was followed by a convincing cup win. The hosts' defensive uncertainty and the visitors' recent improvement make Clermont Foot my selection.", "fc-20261120-12": "Guingamp and Rodez both arrive with uneven results and only one point between them: 14 for the hosts in 11th and 13 for the visitors in 13th. Guingamp beat Clermont and Saint-Etienne without conceding before a heavy loss to Dunkerque. Rodez also won twice before losing their latest league and cup matches. Guingamp's cup exit came on penalties and should be distinguished from a playing-time defeat. This is close, but the hosts' recent evidence of clean-sheet wins and home advantage make Guingamp my selection.", "fc-20261120-13": "Metz's league win at Montpellier gives them attacking encouragement despite a subsequent cup defeat. Seventh on 17 points, they can maintain pressure on the upper places. Boulogne are 12th on 13 and have drawn seven of 12 league matches, suggesting they can frustrate opponents. Their clean-sheet win over Annecy was positive, though they also lost in the cup. Metz must stay patient and protect against counters rather than chase an early breakthrough recklessly. Home advantage and their recent league scoring performance make Metz my selection.", "fc-20261120-14": "Nancy's four consecutive league wins provide the strongest platform in this match. Second on 25 points, they kept clean sheets against Laval and Sochaux. Their cup advancement came through a shootout after a draw and should not be counted as a playing-time win, but the league sequence remains impressive. Dijon are sixth on 18 points and have beaten Grenoble and Red Star in their last two league fixtures. They remain a threat, although a cup loss and earlier league defeats show less consistency. Nancy's sustained league form and home advantage make Nancy my selection.", "fc-20261120-15": "Red Star's cup win does not erase four consecutive league defeats. Eighth on 17 points, they have struggled to score while their defence has been under pressure. Pau are fifth on 20 points and beat Guingamp, Grenoble and Metz in successive league matches before losing to Nantes. They responded with a convincing cup win. The hosts may take encouragement from their own cup result, but the visitors have shown more reliable league scoring and winning form. Pau are my selection.", "fc-20261121-01": "City must respond to three successive league defeats. Their five competitive games brought ten goals conceded, while Fulham conceded only three in five and drew with Newcastle last time. Maresca's confirmation that Marc Guehi is available helps the hosts, but patience and defensive balance remain essential. Home advantage and their chance creation give Manchester City a narrow preference.", "fc-20261121-02": "Villa's 4-4 draw at United showed attacking promise and serious defensive problems. They have only one win in five, while Sunderland arrive after beating Chelsea without conceding. The visitors deserve respect, but Villa's attacking response and home advantage give the hosts a cautious preference.", "fc-20261121-03": "Bournemouth have won five competitive games in a row, scoring 13 and conceding two. Forest's win over City is a warning against complacency, but the hosts have the more sustained record. Scott and Kroupi's availability helps Marco Rose, while Forest lack Hudson-Odoi. Bournemouth are the selection.", "fc-20261121-04": "Chelsea need sharper finishing after losing to Sunderland; their last five brought only five goals. Leeds beat Tottenham but scored just three in five themselves. Caicedo is available, although Chelsea retain several absences. A tight contest is likely, with home advantage favouring Chelsea.", "fc-20261121-05": "Both clubs are near the bottom. Coventry scored and conceded nine in five, while Palace scored only three. Thomas Frank's first match may bring a response, but Mateta's suspension and Sarr's injury limit the visitors. Coventry's greater recent attacking output and home advantage earn a narrow preference.", "fc-20261121-06": "Tottenham's defeat at Leeds followed three consecutive wins and should not erase their defensive improvement: only three conceded in five. Ipswich have gone four without a win. Savio and Bergvall are available again, although Tel remains out. Tottenham's stronger balance at home makes them the selection.", "fc-20261121-07": "Newcastle have only one win in five. Arsenal lead with 27 points and conceded only twice in their last five competitive games. Saliba is available again, but Zubimendi and Saka are out. The hosts can make this uncomfortable, yet Arsenal's defensive consistency makes them the selection.", "fc-20261121-08": "Como's loss to Inter ended four straight wins; they still scored 15 in five. Cagliari stopped four defeats by beating Frosinone, but conceded 12 across that five-game run. Como's stronger attacking record and home advantage make them the selection.", "fc-20261121-09": "Lazio remain top on 29 points after drawing with Napoli, with four wins and a draw in five and 14 goals scored. Lecce stopped three defeats by drawing with Torino but remain winless in four. The hosts' consistency and attacking output favour Lazio.", "fc-20261121-10": "Parma have only one win in five and eight league points. Roma beat Sassuolo without conceding and scored 17 in five, although ten conceded show that their defence is not secure. Their greater attacking threat and third-place standing give Roma the preference.", "fc-20261121-11": "Only one point separates these teams, and both are winless in three. Napoli's draw with leaders Lazio was encouraging, although 11 conceded in five remain a concern. Torino have also struggled for consistency. Napoli receive a narrow home preference rather than a strong endorsement.", "fc-20261121-12": "Alaves' six-goal cup win should not erase the four winless matches before it. Deportivo are unbeaten in three and conceded only three in five. With the visitors ninth on 15 points and more defensively reliable, Deportivo receive a cautious preference.", "fc-20261121-13": "Rayo's defeat at Sociedad followed two wins. Valencia's six-goal cup success should be distinguished from their league defeat by Real Madrid and 19th-place position. Rayo have the modest table advantage and play at home, earning a cautious preference.", "fc-20261121-14": "Derby intensity reduces the value of table position alone. Sevilla are winless in two, while Betis have won twice and sit eight points ahead. Betis must avoid the defensive lapses seen in their cup game, but recent consistency gives the visitors the preference.", "fc-20261121-15": "Madrid have won five competitive games in a row, scoring 15, and beat Valencia without conceding. Celta's five-goal cup victory followed four winless matches and came in a different competitive context. Madrid's more sustained record and home advantage make them the selection.", "fc-20261121-16": "Leverkusen ended two defeats by beating Cologne, but 11 conceded in five show continuing defensive risk. Paderborn's draw with Frankfurt merits respect; friendly results are excluded from the competitive assessment. Leverkusen receive a home preference, provided they protect space behind their attacks.", "fc-20261121-17": "Gladbach's friendly win is excluded from the competitive assessment. Their four league points and bottom position contrast with Dortmund's 21 points and unbeaten five-match competitive run. The visitors still concede chances, but Dortmund's more consistent results make them the selection.", "fc-20261121-18": "Both teams have 12 points and conceded five in their last five. Frankfurt are unbeaten in three, while Hoffenheim responded by beating Schalke but remain inconsistent. The margins look small; Frankfurt's recent continuity and home advantage earn a narrow preference.", "fc-20261121-19": "Elversberg remain a credible home opponent but conceded 12 in five. Freiburg have won four in a row and kept a clean sheet against Union. The hosts can score, yet Freiburg's stronger recent balance makes the visitors the selection.", "fc-20261121-20": "Union's seven league points and limited scoring are concerns after their goalless defeat at Wolfsburg. Leipzig's friendly is excluded from the assessment; their fourth place and 18 points provide the stronger competitive basis. Leipzig are preferred, with defensive concentration still essential away from home.", "fc-20261121-21": "Schalke have lost three straight and scored once in five. Stuttgart arrive after a clean-sheet win over Bremen and have three wins in five. Away inconsistency remains a risk, but the hosts' limited scoring makes Stuttgart the preference.", "fc-20261121-22": "Nice have won three straight and scored 12 in five, so this is a real test. PSG have won all five, scoring 18 and conceding three. Both can threaten, but PSG's stronger balance at both ends gives the league leaders the preference.", "fc-20261121-23": "Monaco are unbeaten in two and have the stronger league position. Auxerre have lost twice in a row and conceded 12 in five. The visitors can slow the game, but Monaco's more stable record and home advantage make them the selection.", "fc-20261121-24": "Lille are unbeaten in three after beating Rennes and sit second on 21 points. Lyon are fifth but scored only three in five and lost without scoring at Brest. With chances potentially scarce, Lille's recent stability at home gives them the preference.", "fc-20261121-25": "Both clubs have 13 points, but Lens have lost three straight and conceded 16 in five. Toulouse beat Strasbourg and conceded only five across their last five. The hosts can respond, yet the visitors' defensive balance gives Toulouse a cautious preference.", "fc-20261121-26": "Strasbourg have lost four of five and conceded 12. Brest have won their last two, most recently without conceding against Lyon, and scored 11 while allowing four in five. The visitors' stronger form at both ends makes Brest the selection.", "fc-20261121-27": "Norwich's five-goal win over Bristol City extended a four-match winning run. Cardiff scored five against Burnley but conceded four, illustrating their defensive risk. Norwich's better recent balance and home advantage make them the selection.", "fc-20261121-28": "Millwall have lost their last two, most recently without scoring at West Brom. QPR beat Lincoln and are unbeaten in two, although nine conceded in five reveal defensive risk. Their stronger table position and recent response earn QPR a cautious preference.", "fc-20261121-29": "Southampton's defeat to Preston was poor, but it followed four unbeaten games. Derby ended four winless matches by beating Bolton, yet remain 23rd with ten points and 11 conceded in five. The hosts' stronger overall balance favours Southampton.", "fc-20261121-30": "Portsmouth's loss to Stoke followed four unbeaten matches. Bolton have only one win in five and conceded 11, compared with Portsmouth's five. Home pressure is a factor, but the visitors' stronger defensive continuity makes Portsmouth the selection.", "fc-20261121-31": "Both sides have 29 points and three successive wins. Stoke conceded only two in five; Birmingham scored 11 while conceding three. This is a close contest between strong teams. Birmingham receive only a marginal preference for their greater attacking output.", "fc-20261121-32": "Lincoln have lost three straight. Wrexham drew with Wolves and are unbeaten in two, conceding only five in their last five. The hosts urgently need points, but urgency does not remove their defensive problems. Wrexham's better balance earns a cautious preference.", "fc-20261121-33": "Swansea sit sixth but have lost four of five and conceded 11. West Brom are unbeaten in five, scoring 11 and most recently beating Millwall without conceding. The table gap is small; the form gap favours West Brom.", "fc-20261121-34": "Middlesbrough are second with 29 points and scored ten in five, despite going winless in their last two. Bristol City arrive after a five-goal loss to Norwich and two straight defeats. The hosts' stronger attacking base and home advantage favour Middlesbrough.", "fc-20261121-35": "West Ham are winless in four and cannot treat the bottom club lightly. Preston beat Southampton without conceding, but that followed four winless games and they still have only eight points. Both carry risk; West Ham receive a cautious home preference.", "fc-20261121-36": "Wolves are unbeaten in five and conceded only three, holding fourth place on 28 points. Charlton's win over Sheffield United ended four defeats but does not erase ten conceded in five. Wolves' sustained defensive and results record makes them the selection.", "fc-20261121-37": "Sheffield United's loss to Charlton ended four unbeaten games. Watford held Middlesbrough goalless and conceded only four in five, so the hosts may need patience. Sheffield United's three wins in five and home advantage earn a narrow preference."});
Object.assign(E.summary,{"fc-20261120-01": "Espanyol's last two clean sheets demand patient attacking play. Athletic have won three of five competitive matches and hold the stronger league position, giving the hosts the edge at San Mames. Athletic need patient possession to draw Espanyol out of their defensive shape. Athletic Club are my selection.", "fc-20261120-02": "Cologne are winless in four league matches and have struggled away. Despite several injuries, Bayern's unbeaten league record, powerful home attack and Kompany's return strongly favour the hosts. Bayern can strengthen their control by restricting Cologne early in possession. Bayern Munich are my selection.", "fc-20261120-03": "Le Havre's five straight defeats and winless league campaign expose a vulnerable defence. Troyes also struggle to score but have shown an ability to keep clean sheets and can make home advantage count. Troyes need to wait for defensive errors without opening up their own back line. Troyes are my selection.", "fc-20261120-04": "Magdeburg carry a dangerous attack and sit three points higher. Bielefeld's successive league wins provide a steadier platform, and disciplined midfield play can help the hosts make home advantage count. Bielefeld must limit Magdeburg in midfield during attacking transitions. Arminia Bielefeld are my selection.", "fc-20261120-05": "Heidenheim's five-match winless sequence limits confidence. Darmstadt face problems at both ends near the bottom, however, leaving the visitors with a narrow advantage based on their stronger season record. Space conceded by Darmstadt could help Heidenheim return to winning ways. 1. FC Heidenheim 1846 are my selection.", "fc-20261120-06": "Molde's scoring power comes with defensive exposure. Bodo/Glimt have won successive league matches and hold a considerably stronger season record, giving them the edge in an open contest. Molde must avoid leaving Bodo/Glimt large spaces in an exchange of attacks. Bodo/Glimt are my selection.", "fc-20261120-07": "Lyngby can threaten on the counter but have lost three of five. AGF's latest league win came with a clean sheet, and their more controlled recent performances favour the home side. AGF can gain greater control by closing Lyngby's counterattacking routes. AGF are my selection.", "fc-20261120-08": "Westerlo retain attacking ability but have conceded heavily in successive defeats. Cercle's two straight wins, including a clean sheet last time, give the hosts a platform to exploit that defensive weakness. Cercle should press Westerlo without the ball and exploit defensive errors. Cercle Brugge KSV are my selection.", "fc-20261120-09": "Only one point separates these teams despite their different positions. Cesena are competitive, but Verona's three straight clean sheets and five-match unbeaten run give the hosts the stronger foundation. Verona can seek a narrow result if they contain Cesena's responses. Hellas Verona are my selection.", "fc-20261120-10": "Andorra continue to struggle for league points and defensive stability. Leganes are also vulnerable at the back but consecutive cup and league victories give the visitors a narrow recent-form edge. Andorra need better defensive connections to stop Leganes building on their recent wins. Leganés are my selection.", "fc-20261120-11": "Annecy's penalty-shootout cup advancement does not erase two heavy league defeats. Clermont's latest league win came with a clean sheet, giving the lower-ranked visitors an opportunity to take a result. Annecy must first reduce their concessions against an improving Clermont attack. Clermont Foot are my selection.", "fc-20261120-12": "Both sides have recent weaknesses and only one point separates them. Guingamp's clean-sheet wins before their latest league setback, together with home advantage, provide a small edge. Guingamp should close Rodez's counterattacking routes while building home pressure. Guingamp are my selection.", "fc-20261120-13": "Boulogne's many league draws call for patience from Metz. Both teams won their latest league games, but the hosts' attacking display at Montpellier and home advantage give them a slight edge. Metz need patience against Boulogne and precision when clear opportunities arrive. Metz are my selection.", "fc-20261120-14": "Dijon's successive league wins deserve respect. Nancy nevertheless have four straight league victories and a stronger defensive platform, making the second-placed hosts the more convincing choice. Nancy can build on their league sequence by denying Dijon midfield space. AS Nancy Lorraine are my selection.", "fc-20261120-15": "Red Star's cup success sits alongside four straight league defeats. Pau have won three of their last four league games and added a convincing cup victory, providing the stronger recent platform. Red Star must protect the spaces lost in transition, but Pau's recent league record is stronger. Pau are my selection.", "fc-20261121-01": "City must respond to three successive league defeats. Their five competitive games brought ten goals conceded, while Fulham conceded only three in five and drew with Newcastle last time. Maresca's confirmation that Marc Guehi is available helps the hosts, but patience and defensive balance remain essential. Home advantage and their chance creation give Manchester City a narrow preference.", "fc-20261121-02": "Villa's 4-4 draw at United showed attacking promise and serious defensive problems. They have only one win in five, while Sunderland arrive after beating Chelsea without conceding. The visitors deserve respect, but Villa's attacking response and home advantage give the hosts a cautious preference.", "fc-20261121-03": "Bournemouth have won five competitive games in a row, scoring 13 and conceding two. Forest's win over City is a warning against complacency, but the hosts have the more sustained record. Scott and Kroupi's availability helps Marco Rose, while Forest lack Hudson-Odoi. Bournemouth are the selection.", "fc-20261121-04": "Chelsea need sharper finishing after losing to Sunderland; their last five brought only five goals. Leeds beat Tottenham but scored just three in five themselves. Caicedo is available, although Chelsea retain several absences. A tight contest is likely, with home advantage favouring Chelsea.", "fc-20261121-05": "Both clubs are near the bottom. Coventry scored and conceded nine in five, while Palace scored only three. Thomas Frank's first match may bring a response, but Mateta's suspension and Sarr's injury limit the visitors. Coventry's greater recent attacking output and home advantage earn a narrow preference.", "fc-20261121-06": "Tottenham's defeat at Leeds followed three consecutive wins and should not erase their defensive improvement: only three conceded in five. Ipswich have gone four without a win. Savio and Bergvall are available again, although Tel remains out. Tottenham's stronger balance at home makes them the selection.", "fc-20261121-07": "Newcastle have only one win in five. Arsenal lead with 27 points and conceded only twice in their last five competitive games. Saliba is available again, but Zubimendi and Saka are out. The hosts can make this uncomfortable, yet Arsenal's defensive consistency makes them the selection.", "fc-20261121-08": "Como's loss to Inter ended four straight wins; they still scored 15 in five. Cagliari stopped four defeats by beating Frosinone, but conceded 12 across that five-game run. Como's stronger attacking record and home advantage make them the selection.", "fc-20261121-09": "Lazio remain top on 29 points after drawing with Napoli, with four wins and a draw in five and 14 goals scored. Lecce stopped three defeats by drawing with Torino but remain winless in four. The hosts' consistency and attacking output favour Lazio.", "fc-20261121-10": "Parma have only one win in five and eight league points. Roma beat Sassuolo without conceding and scored 17 in five, although ten conceded show that their defence is not secure. Their greater attacking threat and third-place standing give Roma the preference.", "fc-20261121-11": "Only one point separates these teams, and both are winless in three. Napoli's draw with leaders Lazio was encouraging, although 11 conceded in five remain a concern. Torino have also struggled for consistency. Napoli receive a narrow home preference rather than a strong endorsement.", "fc-20261121-12": "Alaves' six-goal cup win should not erase the four winless matches before it. Deportivo are unbeaten in three and conceded only three in five. With the visitors ninth on 15 points and more defensively reliable, Deportivo receive a cautious preference.", "fc-20261121-13": "Rayo's defeat at Sociedad followed two wins. Valencia's six-goal cup success should be distinguished from their league defeat by Real Madrid and 19th-place position. Rayo have the modest table advantage and play at home, earning a cautious preference.", "fc-20261121-14": "Derby intensity reduces the value of table position alone. Sevilla are winless in two, while Betis have won twice and sit eight points ahead. Betis must avoid the defensive lapses seen in their cup game, but recent consistency gives the visitors the preference.", "fc-20261121-15": "Madrid have won five competitive games in a row, scoring 15, and beat Valencia without conceding. Celta's five-goal cup victory followed four winless matches and came in a different competitive context. Madrid's more sustained record and home advantage make them the selection.", "fc-20261121-16": "Leverkusen ended two defeats by beating Cologne, but 11 conceded in five show continuing defensive risk. Paderborn's draw with Frankfurt merits respect; friendly results are excluded from the competitive assessment. Leverkusen receive a home preference, provided they protect space behind their attacks.", "fc-20261121-17": "Gladbach's friendly win is excluded from the competitive assessment. Their four league points and bottom position contrast with Dortmund's 21 points and unbeaten five-match competitive run. The visitors still concede chances, but Dortmund's more consistent results make them the selection.", "fc-20261121-18": "Both teams have 12 points and conceded five in their last five. Frankfurt are unbeaten in three, while Hoffenheim responded by beating Schalke but remain inconsistent. The margins look small; Frankfurt's recent continuity and home advantage earn a narrow preference.", "fc-20261121-19": "Elversberg remain a credible home opponent but conceded 12 in five. Freiburg have won four in a row and kept a clean sheet against Union. The hosts can score, yet Freiburg's stronger recent balance makes the visitors the selection.", "fc-20261121-20": "Union's seven league points and limited scoring are concerns after their goalless defeat at Wolfsburg. Leipzig's friendly is excluded from the assessment; their fourth place and 18 points provide the stronger competitive basis. Leipzig are preferred, with defensive concentration still essential away from home.", "fc-20261121-21": "Schalke have lost three straight and scored once in five. Stuttgart arrive after a clean-sheet win over Bremen and have three wins in five. Away inconsistency remains a risk, but the hosts' limited scoring makes Stuttgart the preference.", "fc-20261121-22": "Nice have won three straight and scored 12 in five, so this is a real test. PSG have won all five, scoring 18 and conceding three. Both can threaten, but PSG's stronger balance at both ends gives the league leaders the preference.", "fc-20261121-23": "Monaco are unbeaten in two and have the stronger league position. Auxerre have lost twice in a row and conceded 12 in five. The visitors can slow the game, but Monaco's more stable record and home advantage make them the selection.", "fc-20261121-24": "Lille are unbeaten in three after beating Rennes and sit second on 21 points. Lyon are fifth but scored only three in five and lost without scoring at Brest. With chances potentially scarce, Lille's recent stability at home gives them the preference.", "fc-20261121-25": "Both clubs have 13 points, but Lens have lost three straight and conceded 16 in five. Toulouse beat Strasbourg and conceded only five across their last five. The hosts can respond, yet the visitors' defensive balance gives Toulouse a cautious preference.", "fc-20261121-26": "Strasbourg have lost four of five and conceded 12. Brest have won their last two, most recently without conceding against Lyon, and scored 11 while allowing four in five. The visitors' stronger form at both ends makes Brest the selection.", "fc-20261121-27": "Norwich's five-goal win over Bristol City extended a four-match winning run. Cardiff scored five against Burnley but conceded four, illustrating their defensive risk. Norwich's better recent balance and home advantage make them the selection.", "fc-20261121-28": "Millwall have lost their last two, most recently without scoring at West Brom. QPR beat Lincoln and are unbeaten in two, although nine conceded in five reveal defensive risk. Their stronger table position and recent response earn QPR a cautious preference.", "fc-20261121-29": "Southampton's defeat to Preston was poor, but it followed four unbeaten games. Derby ended four winless matches by beating Bolton, yet remain 23rd with ten points and 11 conceded in five. The hosts' stronger overall balance favours Southampton.", "fc-20261121-30": "Portsmouth's loss to Stoke followed four unbeaten matches. Bolton have only one win in five and conceded 11, compared with Portsmouth's five. Home pressure is a factor, but the visitors' stronger defensive continuity makes Portsmouth the selection.", "fc-20261121-31": "Both sides have 29 points and three successive wins. Stoke conceded only two in five; Birmingham scored 11 while conceding three. This is a close contest between strong teams. Birmingham receive only a marginal preference for their greater attacking output.", "fc-20261121-32": "Lincoln have lost three straight. Wrexham drew with Wolves and are unbeaten in two, conceding only five in their last five. The hosts urgently need points, but urgency does not remove their defensive problems. Wrexham's better balance earns a cautious preference.", "fc-20261121-33": "Swansea sit sixth but have lost four of five and conceded 11. West Brom are unbeaten in five, scoring 11 and most recently beating Millwall without conceding. The table gap is small; the form gap favours West Brom.", "fc-20261121-34": "Middlesbrough are second with 29 points and scored ten in five, despite going winless in their last two. Bristol City arrive after a five-goal loss to Norwich and two straight defeats. The hosts' stronger attacking base and home advantage favour Middlesbrough.", "fc-20261121-35": "West Ham are winless in four and cannot treat the bottom club lightly. Preston beat Southampton without conceding, but that followed four winless games and they still have only eight points. Both carry risk; West Ham receive a cautious home preference.", "fc-20261121-36": "Wolves are unbeaten in five and conceded only three, holding fourth place on 28 points. Charlton's win over Sheffield United ended four defeats but does not erase ten conceded in five. Wolves' sustained defensive and results record makes them the selection.", "fc-20261121-37": "Sheffield United's loss to Charlton ended four unbeaten games. Watford held Middlesbrough goalless and conceded only four in five, so the hosts may need patience. Sheffield United's three wins in five and home advantage earn a narrow preference."});
Object.assign(E.special,{"fc-20261120-02": "Bayern's appeal extends beyond their reputation. Six wins and three draws from nine league games, with 29 goals scored and nine conceded, show a strong balance. Three wins and a draw at home have produced 20 goals, meaning Cologne must withstand repeated pressure rather than isolated attacks. The visitors are winless in four league games and have lost all three away league fixtures this season. Bayern's absentees, including Neuer, Gnabry, Davies, Diaz and Saibari, matter, but Musiala may return and Kompany is back on the touchline. Cologne have counterattacking threats, yet defensive absences including Hubers and Van den Berg further complicate their task. Patient possession, effective counterpressing and sustained chance creation should allow Bayern to convert territorial control into a result. Bayern Munich are my special selection.", "fc-20261120-14": "Nancy's selection rests on the substance of four straight league wins, rather than second place alone. They have found ways to win different kinds of matches: beating Annecy, keeping Laval scoreless, scoring freely against Red Star and then shutting out Sochaux. Dijon deserve respect after successive league wins over Grenoble and Red Star, but earlier defeats to Reims and Rodez and a cup loss to Orleans show a less secure sequence. Nancy's own cup advancement must be described accurately: it came on penalties after a draw, not a fifth playing-time win. The hosts should protect midfield space and prevent Dijon's recent attacking improvement from turning the match into an uncontrolled exchange. With a seven-point league advantage, consistent league results and home support, Nancy have the stronger platform. Nancy are my special selection.", "fc-20261121-15": "Madrid need to maintain pressure from second place, and ten wins from twelve league games offer a stronger foundation than reputation alone. Their last five competitive matches were all victories, including meetings with Barcelona and Leipzig, with 15 goals scored and four conceded. The clean-sheet win at Valencia adds evidence of defensive control. Celta's five-goal cup win restores confidence, but their four preceding matches brought no victories and only one goal. Seven draws from twelve league matches nevertheless show that they can keep contests close. Their route to a result is to protect central space, slow Madrid's attacks and exploit impatience if the hosts do not score early. Madrid must therefore vary their tempo rather than commit too many players forward. Their recent success away from home, greater attacking production and return to home surroundings provide the stronger overall case. Real Madrid are the selection.", "fc-20261121-17": "Competition context matters here. Gladbach's victory over Standard Liege was a friendly and is excluded from their competitive form. Their official run includes wins over Stuttgart and in the cup, but a draw with Paderborn and defeat at Hamburg show that the improvement has not been sustained. One win, one draw and seven league defeats leave them bottom on four points. Dortmund are unbeaten in nine league games, with six wins and three draws for 21 points. Their last five competitive games brought four wins and a draw, including a point away at Bayern and victories over Betis and Elversberg. They are not defensively secure: six conceded in five, including one in each of the last two, give Gladbach a route into the game. The hosts can use an early goal and crowd pressure to change the contest, but their need to push forward may also create transition space. Dortmund must withstand that opening response and remain patient. Their sustained competitive record and greater ability to collect points across different match situations make Borussia Dortmund the selection."});
var ENGLISH_NEWS={
'milan-20261106':["Milan's European hopes take another blow after San Siro defeat to Ferencvaros","AC Milan lost 2–0 to Ferencvaros at San Siro, with Lenny Joseph scoring twice after half-time. Milan have only three points from four matches, putting greater pressure on their remaining European fixtures.","With Mike Maignan suspended, Torriani started in goal and made important early saves. Milan were ultimately punished for mistakes in possession and were unable to make a late numerical advantage count."],
'celtic-20261106':["Celtic claim their first European points after substitutes change the game","Celtic edged Besiktas 3–2 to collect their first Europa League points of the campaign. Having failed to register a shot on target before the break, they came alive in a much more open second half.","Besiktas struck first, but substitutes Osman and Duran gave Celtic fresh attacking momentum. Duran scored twice, and Celtic found a winning response after conceding a late equaliser."],
'juventus-20261106':["Koopmeiners and Kolo Muani fire Juventus to ten European points","Juventus beat AZ Alkmaar 2–1 away to move to ten points from four Europa League matches. First-half goals from Teun Koopmeiners and Randal Kolo Muani proved decisive.","Kolo Muani played a central role by helping create the opener and scoring Juventus's second. AZ pulled one back late on, but the visitors protected their advantage."],
'palace-20261106':["Camarda rescues a point for ten-man Crystal Palace","Crystal Palace drew 1–1 at home to Hoffenheim thanks to an injury-time equaliser from Camarda. Palace had conceded early and saw Wharton dismissed after a second yellow card, leaving them with a difficult finish.","Pino delivered the cross, Mitchell headed it down and Camarda finished from close range. Henderson also contributed important saves as Palace reached five points at the competition's halfway stage."],
'monaco-20261106':["Monaco beat Nordsjaelland to maintain perfect Conference League record","Monaco defeated Nordsjaelland 2–0, extending their Conference League run to three wins from three. Goals from Dittubatt and Adingra settled the contest for the home side.","Minamino helped create the breakthrough. Monaco continued pressing for a second despite disallowed goals and eventually made the result secure late on."],
'brighton-20261106':["Yalcouye's goal earns Brighton away victory at Getafe","Brighton claimed a 1–0 win away to Getafe in the Conference League, their second victory in three matches. Malick Yalcouye scored the decisive goal in the 64th minute.","It was Yalcouye's fourth goal of the season. Brighton stayed patient, took their opportunity and preserved a clean sheet in a challenging away fixture."],
'everton-20261106':["Grealish ruled out against Coventry as Moyes monitors Branthwaite","Everton manager David Moyes confirmed Jack Grealish will miss the match against Coventry. Branthwaite, substituted with cramp against Newcastle, is being assessed and remains a potential option.","Everton arrive on the back of successive wins over Newcastle and sit seventh in the table. Moyes has praised Dewsbury-Hall's recent form, while Coventry have availability concerns of their own."],
'sevilla-20261106':["Sevilla host Alaves as they seek a return to winning ways","Sevilla face Alaves at the Ramon Sanchez Pizjuan in La Liga's 12th round, scheduled for 21:00 local time on November 6 — 02:30 the next morning in Myanmar.","According to Sevilla's official match preview, the sides have met 46 times in competitive matches, with Sevilla winning 22, drawing 12 and losing 12. Taking chances on the night will matter more than the historical record."],
'bournemouth-20261106':["Three substitutes score as Bournemouth come from behind in Prague","Bournemouth recovered from a goal down to beat Sparta Prague 3–1, maintaining four wins from four matches in their first European campaign. Sparta were reduced to ten players before half-time, changing the balance of the match.","Second-half substitutes Tyler Adams, Evanilson and Ryan each scored. Bournemouth's bench made the difference as all three goalscorers entered after kick-off."],
'chelsea-women-20261106':["Five Chelsea players nominated for FIFPRO Women's World 11","Five Chelsea players — Beever-Jones, Lucy Bronze, Ellie Carpenter, Hannah Hampton and Katie McCabe — have been nominated for the FIFPRO Women's World 11 to be announced on November 9.","The award is determined by players' votes. Chelsea says 6,511 women players across 64 countries participated. Nomination does not mean a player has been named in the final eleven."]
};
Object.assign(ENGLISH_NEWS,{"hot-20261120-01": ["Drone footage of Pochettino's first United training session appears online", "Drone footage of Mauricio Pochettino's first Manchester United training session appeared on YouTube on Thursday. ESPN reported that roughly 12 minutes were posted online.", "Pochettino arrived in Manchester on Wednesday after replacing Michael Carrick. The footage brought attention to external filming just as the new coaching team began work.", "The report describes Pochettino working with one group while others trained under assistant Jesus Perez. United declined to comment.", "The uploader defended the flight as compliant with regulations. That assertion does not establish club approval, and the episode may focus attention on training-ground privacy.", "United visit Liverpool at Anfield on Sunday for Pochettino's first match. The training footage should not be treated as confirmation of the starting lineup."], "hot-20261120-02": ["Juan Mata retires from playing at 38", "Juan Mata announced his retirement from professional football on November 18 at the age of 38, as reported by Reuters and Manchester United.", "The Spanish playmaker's career brought major club and international honours and lasting memories for Chelsea and United supporters.", "United highlighted his equaliser in the 2016 FA Cup final, which helped take the match into extra time before the club won the trophy.", "After leaving England, Mata played in Turkey, Japan and Australia. Retirement closes his playing career, while any future role away from the pitch remains a separate matter.", "No coaching appointment or new club position should be inferred from the retirement announcement."], "hot-20261120-03": ["Aston Villa retain Amadou Onana with a new contract", "Aston Villa announced a new contract for Amadou Onana on November 18, moving the story beyond the stage of reported negotiations.", "Retaining the Belgium midfielder gives Villa greater continuity in a central area of the team. The deal signals confidence rather than guaranteeing immediate results.", "The club also published an interview in which Onana discussed the importance of the faith shown in him.", "Attention now turns to how that stability translates into performances. The official announcement carries more weight than transfer speculation.", "Unverified salary and bonus figures are omitted. The confirmed development is that Onana has signed a new deal with Villa."], "hot-20261120-04": ["Vitor Matos takes over as Strasbourg head coach", "Strasbourg announced Vitor Matos as their new head coach on November 18, replacing Hugo Oliveira. Reuters and French outlets reported the club's confirmation.", "The move from Swansea brings a new league and a new squad for Matos to understand quickly.", "His first sessions and matches will show how much the playing style changes. The appointment itself does not confirm a particular starting formation.", "Strasbourg need to turn the new coach's ideas into performances while balancing immediate pressure with longer-term development.", "The confirmed development is the coaching appointment. Future transfers and results remain open questions."], "hot-20261120-05": ["Bay FC sign England defender Jess Carter", "Bay FC announced Jess Carter's signing on November 18 on a contract through 2028 with an option for 2029.", "The England defender arrives from Gotham with championship experience in international football, at Chelsea and in the NWSL.", "The club said Carter appeared in all 30 of Gotham's 2026 regular-season matches. Her experience at centre back and fullback offers flexibility.", "Carter said she welcomed a new challenge and wanted to earn her teammates' trust. Experience will still need to translate into a strong fit with her new side.", "With the transfer confirmed, attention turns to how Carter strengthens Bay FC's defensive organisation."], "hot-20261120-06": ["Kompany returns to Bayern touchline after treatment", "Bayern confirmed on November 19 that Vincent Kompany would return to the touchline against Cologne after missing five competitive matches while receiving medical treatment.", "The coach said he felt well again and was delighted to be back with the team. The update confirms his return to coaching duties.", "Reassembling players after international duty remains a practical challenge despite the positive results recorded during his absence.", "Bayern still have several injury absentees. Kompany said Jamal Musiala could return to the squad, which is not confirmation of a starting place.", "The Cologne match provides the first opportunity to turn the coach's return into another on-field result."], "hot-20261120-07": ["Haaland embraces greater leadership responsibility", "Erling Haaland said on November 19 that taking greater leadership responsibility at Manchester City felt natural, while stressing that he wanted to lead in his own way.", "The 26-year-old Norway striker is part of City's captaincy group this season. His comments reflect a changing role as he gains experience at the club.", "Haaland said becoming a father had also influenced his willingness to take more responsibility.", "He emphasised that new signings need time and matches to settle. That points to a role in helping the group integrate, alongside his goalscoring duties.", "Upcoming matches will show how that leadership is expressed through communication and the team's responses on the pitch."], "hot-20261120-08": ["Barco believes he can offer Chelsea more", "Valentin Barco told ESPN that he believed he could contribute much more to Chelsea and retained confidence in his ability. The interview was reported on November 19.", "The Argentina international returned to his club without appearing in his country's two latest friendlies. He said he wanted to play while still valuing national-team involvement.", "Despite limited minutes under Xabi Alonso, Barco stressed continued work and improvement rather than resignation.", "His next task is to turn that confidence into training performances and effective contributions when opportunities arrive. An interview cannot guarantee a starting place.", "The comments do not establish a transfer request or a decision to leave Chelsea."], "hot-20261120-09": ["Report: Fulham seek Bassey extension amid United interest", "Sky Sports' November 19 paper review, citing The Athletic, reported that Fulham were pushing to extend Calvin Bassey's contract.", "The report also linked the defender with Manchester United. Interest is not a confirmed bid or transfer agreement.", "A new deal could give Fulham defensive continuity and a stronger negotiating position. That is analysis of the report, not confirmation that a contract is signed.", "No verified transfer fee, salary or agreement date is available here, so none is added.", "Official confirmation from Fulham or the parties involved is still required."], "hot-20261120-10": ["Frank focuses on rebuilding Palace confidence before Coventry", "Thomas Frank is working to restore Crystal Palace's confidence before his first match against Coventry. In comments reported on November 19, he welcomed the energy in training while stressing the need for belief.", "He also joked about the coffee-cup episode from his Tottenham tenure, but Palace's on-field response remains the more important issue.", "Jean-Philippe Mateta remains suspended. Takehiro Tomiyasu is due to resume training next week, while Ismaila Sarr's return to training remains uncertain.", "Frank said he could be flexible with formations to place players in their best positions. A new appointment does not instantly establish a settled system.", "Coventry will provide the first test of whether training-ground energy becomes a stronger competitive performance."], "hot-20261121-01": ["Kane faces months out with ankle ligament injury", "Bayern confirmed on Friday that Harry Kane tore a ligament in his left ankle.", "He was injured against Cologne and examined by the club medical staff.", "The striker is expected to miss the coming months.", "Michael Olise also has a forefoot contusion and will receive treatment.", "No exact return date for Kane has been announced."], "hot-20261121-02": ["Pochettino sets out rebuilding plans at United", "Pochettino wants United to establish a new identity rather than dwell on past failures.", "His first match is at Liverpool.", "Bruno Fernandes remains central as captain.", "Restoring player confidence is a priority.", "Anfield will offer an early test of how quickly his ideas reach the pitch."], "hot-20261121-03": ["Saliba available; Zubimendi and Saka remain out", "Arteta says Saliba is available for Newcastle after recovering from his back injury.", "The defender has completed preparatory matches.", "Zubimendi faces several weeks out with a hamstring injury.", "Saka remains around four weeks away.", "Arsenal gain defensive cover but must adjust midfield and wing selection."], "hot-20261121-04": ["Maresca focuses on football as City seek a response", "Maresca rejects a link between City’s financial case and their slump.", "They face Fulham after three league defeats.", "Avoidable goals are his immediate concern.", "Marc Guehi is available again.", "The next test is restoring defensive balance without losing attacking creativity."], "hot-20261121-05": ["Christensen doubtful after new calf discomfort", "Barcelona say Christensen has discomfort in his left calf and is doubtful for Villarreal.", "The setback follows his recent return from injury.", "Recovery depends on how symptoms develop.", "Flick faces another defensive selection decision.", "Doubtful status does not yet confirm an absence."], "hot-20261121-06": ["CONMEBOL renews its backing for Infantino", "CONMEBOL’s ten associations renewed their support for Infantino on Friday.", "The endorsement followed a council meeting in Barranquilla.", "It sets out South America’s position before the March 2027 election.", "An endorsement is not an election result.", "Other associations’ responses remain relevant."], "hot-20261121-07": ["NWSL final ticket prices remain unusually high", "Resale entry prices for the Spirit–Current final have fallen from their peak.", "They remain high compared with previous NWSL finals, according to Reuters.", "Playing at Audi Field boosts local demand.", "These are changing resale prices, not a single official face value.", "The final highlights both commercial interest and affordability."], "hot-20261121-08": ["Kroupi ready to start as Scott builds minutes", "Marco Rose says Kroupi is ready to start.", "Alex Scott is also ready for increased minutes after injury.", "Rose expects Scott to start at least one of the next three matches.", "Availability does not guarantee a start against Forest.", "Managing minutes will matter during Bournemouth’s busy schedule."], "hot-20261121-09": ["Szoboszlai trains normally before United clash", "Iraola says Szoboszlai has trained normally and is fine.", "That eases concern after his knee problems on international duty.", "Van Dijk, Gravenberch and Frimpong should also be available if progress continues.", "Bradley and Leoni have resumed some training but are not ready to play.", "The final squad will clarify selection."], "hot-20261121-10": ["Nations League draw sets major quarter-final ties", "The Nations League draw on 20 November paired Spain with France.", "Norway will face England, creating a major test for Haaland’s national side.", "Belgium meet Germany and the Netherlands face Portugal.", "The official draw determines the two-legged quarter-final pairings.", "These ties will shape the route towards the finals."]});
Object.assign( E.preview,{"fc-20261116-01":"For Germany, the night in Berlin carries greater weight than a normal home fixture. Third in the group with eight points, they need a positive result against leaders Netherlands and hope to build on a three-goal away win over Serbia. Germany's last five produced two wins, two draws and one defeat, but their inability to score against Greece in two meetings shows that a well-organised defence can still frustrate them. Netherlands lead on eleven points, remain unbeaten in five and recently scored seven against Greece. Germany cannot press with so many players that they leave spaces for the visitors to exploit. Their ability to keep a compact shape while taking control could determine the match. Despite Dutch momentum, Germany's improved finishing in Serbia and the urgency of a home response make **Germany my selection.**","fc-20261116-02":"The central question for Greece is how quickly they can recover from a seven-goal defeat in the Netherlands. Before that collapse they had gone four group games unbeaten, including victory away to Germany, so one disastrous result should not erase their underlying form. Greece still sit second with eight points and have their fate largely in their own hands. Serbia have lost all five group matches and conceded three against Germany most recently. Their first task is therefore to restore defensive stability rather than launch sustained pressure on the hosts. Greece must avoid a reckless attacking response that would expose a shaken back line. If they manage the game patiently and choose their openings, they can punish Serbia's repeated defensive errors. Allowing for the psychological cost of their latest loss, stronger group form and home advantage still make **Greece my selection.**","fc-20261116-03":"North Macedonia remain without a point ahead of their final group match, reflecting persistent problems in both finishing and defending. They scored once away to Scotland but could not prevent defeat, and failed to score in either of their two home fixtures. There is little recent evidence of a quick turnaround. Slovenia sit second on eight points and their latest goalless draw with Switzerland demonstrated an ability to contain even the group leaders. They have also won away to Scotland, so playing on the road is no reason to underestimate them. The hosts may play with added urgency in pursuit of their first point, which means Slovenia should stay patient early on. Even allowing for that final-match motivation, the contrast between five straight Macedonian defeats and Slovenia's steadier results makes **Slovenia my selection.**","fc-20261116-04":"Switzerland have been the group's most reliable side, taking thirteen points from four wins and one draw in five fixtures. They failed to score on their latest visit to Slovenia, but were productive in their previous four matches and have won both home games. Scotland sit third with seven points and travel with confidence after beating North Macedonia, yet defeats to Slovenia and Switzerland illustrate their difficulty against the group's stronger teams. An early Swiss goal could force the visitors to attack more openly and allow the hosts to control proceedings. Scotland must defend carefully at the start and make the most of limited chances. Switzerland's unbeaten record, home results and more effective finishing throughout the campaign make **Switzerland my selection.**","fc-20261116-05":"The Faroe Islands need to turn resilience into victory. They have drawn all five group games, remaining unbeaten but collecting only five points and sitting third. A home win over seven-point Moldova is necessary to climb above the visitors. Their latest two-goal draw away to Slovakia showed they can respond under pressure, although they must now turn chances into decisive goals. Moldova are better placed in the table and will look to make the game uncomfortable for the hosts. A sixth draw would do little to solve the Faroes' problem, but rushing forward could open dangerous spaces. If the home side remain patient, protect possession and use their recent fighting spirit, they have a route to three points. Given the home incentive and competitive record, **Faroe Islands are my selection.**","fc-20261116-06":"Kazakhstan are bottom of their group with two points after five matches and are still searching for a first victory. Defeat away to Moldova again showed their difficulty in turning encouraging draws against the Faroe Islands into sustained progress. Slovakia lead with eleven points, having won three and drawn two without defeat. Their four goals away to Moldova underline a more reliable attacking threat, even if their own defence has occasionally been tested. Kazakhstan will need an organised start and greater precision when opportunities arise; the visitors should avoid taking control for granted. Comparing the sides' ability to create chances, accumulate points and manage difficult away games, **Slovakia are my selection.**","fc-20261116-07":"Estonia have built their campaign around defensive discipline rather than heavy scoring. Two wins and three draws in five matches have earned them nine points, and four consecutive clean sheets give them a strong platform for this home game. Bulgaria have four points and enter after conceding five in their most recent defeat. They will need to find a way through a home defence that has been hard to break down. Estonia are not especially prolific, so patience and careful game management will matter more than taking unnecessary risks in pursuit of an early goal. The hosts' unbeaten record, second-place standing and defensive consistency make **Estonia my selection.**","fc-20261116-08":"Iceland lead the group with eleven points heading into the final fixture and arrive at their most confident attacking moment after scoring five away to Bulgaria. Four consecutive clean sheets show that the lead has not been built on goals alone. Luxembourg won their opener but have since lost four straight games and failed to score in the last three. The visitors, fourth with three points, must avoid conceding early, yet sitting deep for the entire match could simply invite prolonged Icelandic pressure. The hosts still need disciplined preparation rather than assuming the result is secured. Recent finishing, defensive resilience and the clear gap between the teams' group performances all point towards **Iceland as my selection.**","fc-20261116-09":"Lithuania have four points from three group matches and sit second, with a final home fixture offering an opportunity to finish with a victory. A goalless friendly against Suriname showed that they still need to sharpen their attack, but a recent three-goal win over Andorra demonstrates what they can produce on home soil. Liechtenstein have only one group point and failed to score in their last five games, leaving problems at both ends of the pitch. Their goalless away draw with Azerbaijan is a warning that an impatient host can still be frustrated. Lithuania must construct chances carefully and use any lead to control the match. Home advantage and the difference in attacking output make **Lithuania my selection.**","fc-20261116-10":"Gibraltar enter the final group game still seeking their first victory, but must face an unbeaten Malta side. The hosts are third with two points and failed to score in their latest defeat away to Andorra, making a stronger attacking display essential. Malta lead the group with seven points after three wins and two draws in their last five. Victories over Andorra both home and away underline their ability to manage tight games. Gibraltar did earn a draw in Malta, so the visitors cannot afford complacency simply because they lead the table. An organised opening by the hosts could keep the contest close. Nevertheless, Malta's recent winning habits and unbeaten run make **Malta my selection.**","fc-20261116-11":"Albacete's recent form no longer reflects their lowly league position. They remain twenty-first with ten points, yet consecutive league victories over Eldense, Sabadell and Leganes, followed by a three-goal cup performance, show clear momentum. Celta Fortuna are seventeenth on thirteen points but have gone four matches without winning and lost their last two away fixtures, at Girona and Burgos. Conceding five at Girona raises concerns over how they will handle a home attack growing in confidence. Albacete's poor season record should not be ignored, yet their recent conversion of chances has improved markedly. Giving more weight to current direction and home advantage than the table alone, **Albacete are my selection.**"});
Object.assign( E.summary,{"fc-20261116-01":"Netherlands arrive in Berlin unbeaten in five after scoring seven against Greece. Germany regained confidence with an away win over Serbia, but are third on eight points and urgently need a home result. Containing Dutch transitions is crucial; **Germany are my selection.**","fc-20261116-02":"Serbia have lost every group fixture, while Greece remain second with eight points. The heavy defeat in the Netherlands will test Greece's confidence, but their preceding four-match unbeaten run and home advantage favour **Greece.**","fc-20261116-03":"North Macedonia have lost five straight and failed to score in both home matches. Slovenia have eight points, held Switzerland scoreless and won away to Scotland. Their more stable performances make **Slovenia my selection.**","fc-20261116-04":"Scotland arrive after a win, but Switzerland remain unbeaten with four victories from five and have won both home fixtures. Their superior group form and home strength favour **Switzerland.**","fc-20261116-05":"Moldova are two points ahead, so the Faroe Islands need a victory rather than a sixth consecutive draw. Their unbeaten resistance and home motivation give **Faroe Islands my selection.**","fc-20261116-06":"Slovakia lead with three wins and two draws; Kazakhstan remain winless. The visitors also scored four away to Moldova. Recent attacking efficiency and group form favour **Slovakia.**","fc-20261116-07":"Estonia have kept four straight clean sheets and remain unbeaten on nine points, while Bulgaria conceded five in their latest game. Defensive stability and home advantage make **Estonia my selection.**","fc-20261116-08":"Luxembourg have lost four in a row and failed to score in their last three. Iceland lead with eleven points, four successive clean sheets and five goals in their latest win. **Iceland are my selection.**","fc-20261116-09":"Liechtenstein have not scored in five games. Lithuania failed to score in their latest friendly but recently netted three at home against Andorra. A patient approach favours **Lithuania.**","fc-20261116-10":"Malta have three wins and two draws from their last five; Gibraltar lost to Andorra without scoring. Gibraltar drew in Malta, but the visitors' stronger form makes **Malta my selection.**","fc-20261116-11":"Celta Fortuna are winless in four and lost consecutive away games. Albacete have won three straight league fixtures and another cup match. Their improving finishing and home edge make **Albacete my selection.**"});
Object.assign( E.special,{"fc-20261116-03":"North Macedonia have reached the final group game with no points, a record exposing both their lack of cutting edge and repeated defensive lapses. A goal in Scotland offered some encouragement, but the loss continued a five-game losing streak and they have failed to score in two home outings. Slovenia's eight points are more than a statistical advantage: they earned them by restricting Switzerland to a goalless draw and winning away in Scotland. The visitors have demonstrated an ability to defend against stronger teams and stay composed away from home. Macedonia may throw players forward to rescue some pride, potentially creating spaces behind their defensive line. Slovenia should not become impatient if an early goal fails to arrive; the hosts proved in Scotland that they can still threaten on occasion. Over the full ninety minutes, the visitors' greater consistency, better defensive organisation and superior group record offer the stronger case. **Slovenia are my Special Choice.**","fc-20261116-08":"Iceland's case rests on more than the five goals they scored away to Bulgaria. Before that emphatic result, they had beaten Luxembourg and Bulgaria without conceding and navigated a difficult trip to Estonia with a goalless draw. Those performances demonstrate the defensive control required when an opponent frustrates the attack. Iceland now lead on eleven points and have four consecutive clean sheets; Luxembourg, by contrast, have followed their opening win with four straight defeats and three consecutive games without a goal. The visitors may attempt to slow the tempo and defend deep, which would test the hosts' patience and create pressure if the score remains level. Yet Luxembourg's recent lack of attacking output makes it difficult to force Iceland into a more defensive posture. By keeping their shape and building chances methodically, the hosts should have the clearer route to success. **Iceland are my Special Choice.**"});
Object.assign( ENGLISH_NEWS,{"hot-20261116-01":["Ronaldinho returns to professional football at 46 with Ravenna","Ronaldinho's familiar smile has returned to the pitch. The Brazilian great started for Ravenna in Italy's Serie C on November 15, making a return to professional competitive football at the age of 46.","He played the first 45 minutes of the derby against Forli. This was not merely a ceremonial exhibition appearance; he was included in Ravenna's official league starting lineup.","His passing featured in the move that led to the opening goal. That should not be exaggerated into a personal goal or a confirmed final assist, but flashes of his technical ability were visible.","The appearance attracted attention precisely because it came in an official competitive setting rather than a legends' friendly. Any assessment of a longer-term return should await the club's subsequent selection decisions.","For now, the confirmed story is his first-half appearance and contribution to the build-up, not a promise that he will play every forthcoming match."],"hot-20261116-02":["Haaland says he remains happy at Manchester City amid off-field case","Erling Haaland has addressed questions about his future while Manchester City's off-field legal proceedings continue. Speaking after international duty, the Norway forward said he remains happy at City and focused on his football.","Asked how possible sanctions might affect him, Haaland separated his own position from the dispute between the Premier League and the club. He said he did not know its legal details.","His comments are not confirmation of any legal ruling. He also pointed to his long-term contract and commitment to the team rather than announcing an intention to leave.","For City supporters, the remarks offer a clearer view of their striker's present priorities without settling the underlying proceedings.","Any conclusion about the case or a potential transfer must be based on a separate official development, not inferred from this interview."],"hot-20261116-03":["Klopp criticises Infantino's FIFA leadership and calls for change","Germany coach Jurgen Klopp has criticised FIFA president Gianni Infantino's leadership. At a news conference before the Netherlands match, he expressed the view that a change at the top of world football would be appropriate.","Klopp's central argument was that the game's interests should take precedence over financial considerations in FIFA's leadership.","These were his opinions and criticism, not an announcement that FIFA had decided to remove its president.","He did not confirm a replacement candidate, a resignation, or a newly concluded election outcome. Those events would require separate official confirmation.","The comments nevertheless add a prominent coaching voice to the debate about how international football should be governed."],"hot-20261116-04":["Maignan to undergo checks at Milan after being withdrawn against Turkey","AC Milan are monitoring Mike Maignan's fitness after the France goalkeeper was replaced at half-time during the Nations League match against Turkey because of discomfort around his hip.","Guillaume Restes replaced him, and the France medical staff have communicated with Milan's doctors ahead of an assessment when he returns to the club.","The crucial uncertainty is the severity and duration of the problem. Discomfort alone does not establish a long absence, nor does it prove the issue is minor.","Milan's immediate priority is to obtain a clear medical assessment before deciding how to manage their first-choice goalkeeper.","An estimate of matches missed should wait for the test results and an official update. No definite recovery timetable has yet been confirmed."],"hot-20261116-05":["Szoboszlai reveals knee concern nearly kept him out before Georgia match","Dominik Szoboszlai played the full ninety minutes against Georgia, but admitted he had doubts about taking part before kick-off. He felt discomfort during a shooting action in the warm-up.","The Hungary captain had been training with support around his knee. He went on to play and contributed an assist in his team's victory.","Completing the game does not establish that the problem has disappeared. Szoboszlai said treatment would resume as he prepares for the next fixture.","With Hungary approaching a decisive group match against Northern Ireland, the midfielder's availability matters to both his national side and Liverpool.","Further training sessions and medical assessments should clarify whether he is ready. Claims that he is fully fit or definitely ruled out would currently go beyond the confirmed information."],"hot-20261116-06":["Alphonso Davies set to return to Munich after Canada injury","Bayern Munich defender Alphonso Davies is expected to return to Munich after sustaining an injury during international duty with Canada. Reports citing a Canada Soccer spokesperson say he will miss the next match against Guatemala.","Davies slipped early in the first Guatemala game and tried to continue, before signalling to the bench that he needed to be substituted. The information confirmed so far describes a lower-body injury.","There is concern about a possible recurrence of a muscular problem, but that possibility is not a final medical diagnosis.","Because the full-back depends heavily on acceleration and running power, Bayern will need to manage any return carefully after evaluating him.","No precise length of absence has been confirmed. Missing Canada's next game should not automatically be treated as confirmation that he will miss a particular number of Bayern fixtures."],"hot-20261116-07":["Frenkie de Jong left out of Netherlands trip to Berlin as precaution","Netherlands will be without Frenkie de Jong for their decisive meeting with Germany. The midfielder was left out of the Berlin trip as a precaution after experiencing minor discomfort following the match against Greece, according to reports citing the Dutch federation.","De Jong had returned to international duty against Greece and even wore the captain's armband during the first half.","Coach Xavi has opted not to call up an additional replacement. The confirmed absence concerns the Germany match; it is not evidence of a lengthy layoff at Barcelona.","Without De Jong's ability to retain the ball and escape midfield pressure, the Netherlands must adjust their plans for a demanding away fixture.","The matchday selection and subsequent club fitness updates will clarify the impact. The precautionary decision should not be presented as proof of a serious injury."],"hot-20261116-08":["Mary Fowler and Kyra Cooney-Cross return to Australia's squad for Colombia friendlies","Mary Fowler and Kyra Cooney-Cross have returned to Australia's women's national squad. They are among six recalled players in the November 16 selection for two friendlies against Colombia.","Goalkeeper Teagan Micah also returns after missing time following a head injury. Fowler and Alanna Kennedy were among the players absent from the October international window.","The matches are scheduled for November 28 in Canberra and December 2 in Geelong. Selection in the squad expands the coach's options but does not guarantee a starting place.","The two fixtures are an important stage in preparations for the 2027 Women's World Cup, allowing coach Joe Montemurro to assess returning experienced players alongside current performers.","Training progress, Micah's return and the way Fowler is integrated will be key storylines ahead of the opening game."],"hot-20261116-09":["Andy Robertson one appearance away from moving past Kenny Dalglish","Scotland captain Andy Robertson could make history against Switzerland. A UEFA preview published on November 15 noted that a 103rd senior international appearance would give him a new national record.","Robertson reached 102 caps against North Macedonia, drawing level with Kenny Dalglish. Another appearance would move him clear.","The milestone has not yet occurred simply because the next match is scheduled. He must actually take the field for cap number 103 to be confirmed.","Sustaining a lengthy international career demands not only ability but fitness, consistency and repeated selection over many seasons.","Scotland's team result and Robertson's personal milestone will be watched together. The official match record should be checked afterwards before reporting that the record has been broken."],"hot-20261116-10":["Ibrahim Maza sidelined by ankle injury as Leverkusen await assessment","Bayer Leverkusen midfielder Ibrahim Maza has suffered an ankle injury while representing Algeria. An update attributed to the Algerian football federation on November 15 confirms he will miss the next match against Togo.","The injury occurred in the first meeting with Togo. The confirmed issue is an ankle sprain that prevents his involvement in the following international fixture.","The available report does not set out an exact recovery period. It would therefore be premature to conclude he will definitely miss Leverkusen's next club match.","Leverkusen will need to assess the extent of the injury and determine when the midfielder can return to training before making plans.","His international absence is confirmed; his club availability remains dependent on further evaluation and should be reported separately."]});
